\ls2\ilvl0\cf2 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Due to the 
\f1\b non-reproducibility
\f0\b0  of the 
\f1\b LDA model
\f0\b0 , 
\f1\b rerunning
\f0\b0  Topic_Modeling_LDA_Mallet.ipynb will 
\f1\b retrain the model
\f0\b0 , which will result in differences between the newly generated analysis images and the original ones we used.\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}If you want to 
\f1\b retrain the LDA model
\f0\b0 , in addition to replacing the 
\f1\b data input and output paths
\f0\b0  in the 
\f1\b Topic_Modeling_LDA_Mallet.ipynb
\f0\b0  file, you also need to update the 
\f1\b Mallet file path
\f0\b0  in the 
\f1\b mallet_path function
\f0\b0 .\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}The 
\f1\b Mallet file path
\f0\b0  is located in the folder: 
\f1\b ~/mallet-2.0.8/mallet-2.0.8/bin/mallet
\f0\b0 .\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}If you only need to 
\f1\b repeat the data results
\f0\b0 , you only need to 
\f1\b replace the model input path and result output path
\f0\b0 .\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}The model is stored in the 
\f1\b PKL folder
\f0\b0 \uc0\u65306 
\f1\b dictionary.dict
\f0\b0  is the 
\f1\b vocabulary collection
\f0\b0  generated during 
\f1\b model training
\f0\b0 .\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}lda_model is the model we used in this analysis\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}ldamallet.pkl is a 
\f1\b serialized (pickled) version
\f0\b0  of the trained 
\f1\b LDA Mallet model
\f0\b0  which contains 
\f1\b topic distributions, word-topic assignments, and all model parameters
\f0\b0 .\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}The remaining 
\f1\b folders and files
\f0\b0  contain 
\f1\b results generated
\f0\b0  from partial executions, including 
\f1\b PNG, HTML, and other formats
\f0\b0 .\
